vice</resTitle><date><pubDate>2016-03-28</pubDate></date><citRespParty><rpOrgName>Montana State Library</rpOrgName><role><RoleCd value="006"/></role></citRespParty><citOnlineRes><linkage>http://gisservicemt.gov/arcgis/rest/services/MSDI_Framework</linkage></citOnlineRes></aggrDSName><assocType><AscTypeCd value="002"/></assocType></aggrInfo><spatRpType><SpatRepTypCd value="003" Sync="TRUE"></SpatRepTypCd></spatRpType><dataLang><languageCode value="eng"/><countryCode value="USA" Sync="TRUE"/></dataLang><dataExt xmlns=""><geoEle xmlns=""><GeoBndBox><westBL>-116.178571</westBL><eastBL>-103.611177</eastBL><southBL>44.316161</southBL><northBL>49.180871</northBL></GeoBndBox></geoEle><exDesc>bounding box</exDesc></dataExt><dataExt xmlns=""><exDesc>publication date</exDesc><tempEle><TempExtent><exTemp><TM_Instant><tmPosition>2026-05-06T00:00:00</tmPosition></TM_Instant></exTemp></TempExtent></tempEle></dataExt><suppInfo>These data represent Montana's School Districts boundaries. All Montana County School District Superintendents were contacted for legal descriptions/source documents. Montana law requires all County School District Superintendent to have these documents available for the public. The boundary files were created based on the best available source data received from the counties: Legal Descriptions, County GIS Files, County Source Maps, or where data sources were not available the Montana Cadastral GIS Data was used. Digital data used as a base layer to create these boundary files were the best available source at the time: Cadastral (parcel lines), Geographic Coordination Data Base (GCDB), National Agriculture Imagery Program (NAIP) Imagery, and 1:24,000 USGS Topographic Maps. All of these base layers can be found at the Montana State Library's website. The Montana State Library (MSL) and the MSDI supports a federated database approach to all MSDI layers. Montana defines a federated approach as a method that supports the integration and utilization of data from multiple data providers, while retaining the primary maintenance responsibility with the provider. Most of Montana's framework data model efforts have adopted a federated approach that leverages multiple data providers and thus multiple data maintainers. It is plausible that errors do exist and we welcome all corrections. If you do have a correction to a school district boundary or attribute information please contact the Administrative Boundaries Framework Coordinator.</suppInfo><dataChar><CharSetCd value="004"/></dataChar><envirDesc Sync="TRUE"> Version 6.2 (Build 9200) ; Esri ArcGIS 10.7.1.11595</envirDesc><idCredit>Office of Public Instruction, Montana State Library</idCredit><tpCat><TopicCatCd value="017"/></tpCat><tpCat><TopicCatCd value="003"/></tpCat></dataIdInfo><mdMaint><maintFreq><MaintFreqCd value="009"/></maintFreq></mdMaint><spatRepInfo><VectSpatRep><geometObjs Name="DBO.BNDY_SchoolDistrict_ElementaryLines"><geoObjTyp><GeoObjTypCd value="002" Sync="TRUE"/></geoObjTyp><geoObjCnt Sync="TRUE">2199</geoObjCnt></geometObjs><topLvl><TopoLevCd value="001" Sync="TRUE"/></topLvl></VectSpatRep></spatRepInfo><refSysInfo><RefSystem><refSysID><identCode code="32100" Sync="TRUE"/><idCodeSpace Sync="TRUE">EPSG</idCodeSpace><idVersion Sync="TRUE">4.5(3.0.1)</idVersion></refSysID></RefSystem></refSysInfo><eainfo><detailed Name="SchoolDistrict_CntySupt"><enttyp><enttypl Sync="TRUE">SchoolDistrict_CntySupt</enttypl><enttypt Sync="TRUE">Table</enttypt><enttypc Sync="TRUE">0</enttypc></enttyp><attr><attrlabl Sync="TRUE">OID</attrlabl><attalias Sync="TRUE">OID</attalias><attrtype Sync="TRUE">OID</attrtype><attwidth Sync="TRUE">4</attwidth><atprecis Sync="TRUE">0</atprecis><attscale Sync="TRUE">0</attscale><attrdef Sync="TRUE">Internal feature number.</attrdef><attrdefs Sync="TRUE">Esri</attrdefs><attrdomv><udom Sync="TRUE">Sequential unique whole numbers that are automatically generated.</udom></attrdomv></attr><attr><attrlabl Sync="TRUE">NAME</attrlabl><attalias Sync="TRU